WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.889
CHIATECH JOURNAL explanatory summary: Tailoring Techniques for Special-Occasion Dresses in Berom Land: A Case Study of Jos South Local Government Area, Plateau State, Nigeria

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:22.000
Article focus: Background: Berom special-occasion dress sits at the intersection of indigenous textile identity and made-to-measure garment engineering.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Research context: Purpose: This study examined culturally responsive tailoring techniques for special-occasion dresses in Berom land, using Jos South Local Government Area, Plateau State, Nigeria, as a case study.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Study approach: Methods: A convergent mixed-method field-audit and documentary case-study design combined a criterion-based audit of 17 tailoring/fashion enterprises conducted on 16 August 2026 with structured coding of eight directly relevant empirical cultural and apparel sources.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:06.889
Reported findings: Frequencies, percentages, mean, median and structured content coding were used; the field and documentary evidence streams were kept analytically distinct.

00:01:06.889 --> 00:01:15.222
Interpretation: Results: Thirteen of the 17 enterprises (76.5%) were categorized as fashion designers.

00:01:15.222 --> 00:01:24.444
Publication record: e003 · Volume 1, Issue 1 · July 2026 Pioneer Issue. DOI pending registration.
